description:
## Why

Second foundation piece for PKIX-baac. SCT signature verification (child C) needs the log's public key keyed by log_id; the log list is where that comes from.

## What

A pluggable `CtLogList` type that maps log_id (SHA-256 of pubkey DER, 32 bytes) → log public key DER. Plus a loader for Google/Chrome's log_list.json schema.

**Google log_list.json schema** (https://www.gstatic.com/ct/log_list/v3/log_list.json):

```json
{
  "operators": [
    {
      "name": "Google",
      "logs": [
        {
          "description": "Google 'Argon2024' log",
          "log_id": "<base64 SHA-256(pubkey)>",
          "key": "<base64 DER subjectPublicKeyInfo>",
          "url": "https://ct.googleapis.com/logs/argon2024/",
          "state": { "usable": { "timestamp": "..." } },
          "temporal_interval": { ... }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

## Public API

```rust
pub struct CtLogList {
    logs: BTreeMap<[u8; 32], CtLog>,
}

pub struct CtLog {
    pub log_id: [u8; 32],
    pub key_der: Vec<u8>,          // SubjectPublicKeyInfo
    pub description: alloc::string::String,
    pub url: alloc::string::String,
    pub usable_from_ms: Option<u64>,
    pub retired_at_ms: Option<u64>,
}

impl CtLogList {
    pub fn new() -> Self;
    pub fn insert(&mut self, log: CtLog);
    pub fn get(&self, log_id: &[u8; 32]) -> Option<&CtLog>;
    pub fn len(&self) -> usize;
    pub fn is_empty(&self) -> bool;

    /// Parse Chrome/Google log_list.json schema v3.
    /// Behind feature 'log-list-json' so the core crate stays no_std + zero JSON deps.
    #[cfg(feature = "log-list-json")]
    pub fn from_google_log_list_json(json: &str) -> Result<Self, Error>;
}
```

The JSON loader gets its own feature flag — keep the core `CtLogList` no_std with no JSON deps. Consumers who don't want JSON can populate via `insert()` directly.

## Validation

- log_id MUST equal SHA-256(pubkey_der) — verify this when inserting; reject mismatches.
- `state.usable.timestamp` (ms since epoch) → `usable_from_ms` for time-windowed validation later.

## Test fixtures + oracle

Fetch a current log_list.json snapshot into `pkix-ct/tests/fixtures/log_list_v3_snapshot.json` with a one-line provenance comment in the test file. Independent oracle: Chrome's published list — what we parse must match Chrome's view.

## Acceptance

- [ ] `CtLogList` with insert/get/len/is_empty.
- [ ] log_id ⇔ SHA-256(pubkey_der) consistency check enforced.
- [ ] `from_google_log_list_json` parses a real snapshot, behind feature `log-list-json`.
- [ ] Tests parse the snapshot and assert log count, look up at least 3 known log_ids by their public-record SHA-256.

## Effort

~150 lines + tests. ~half a day.

## Filed as

Child .2 of PKIX-baac per its recommended decomposition.
